    "text": "96\n\n Think Your Non-Compete Doesn\u2019t Matter? Think Again.\nHi Sara,\nLet\u2019s talk about the number one clause that gets glossed over, shrugged off, and misunderstood in nearly every deal I touch: the non-compete.\nEvery day, I hear some version of: \u201cNon-competes aren\u2019t enforceable, right? So who cares?\u201d\nOh, just the buyer, the seller, the bank, and your entire deal. That\u2019s who.\nThe Non-Compete Myth That Won\u2019t Die\nThanks to headlines (and let\u2019s be honest, a few clickbaity TikToks), people think non-competes are dead. But here\u2019s the truth: they\u2019re very much alive\u2014especially when you\u2019re buying or selling a business.\nEven when the FTC tried to come for them, they carved out a big juicy exception for business sales. Why? Because you can\u2019t buy an accounting firm and then let the seller open a competing firm across the street the next day. That's not a business deal. That's a mess.\nWhere Your Non-Compete Lives Matters\nIt\u2019s not just what your non-compete says, but where it lives. Stick it in the wrong agreement\u2014say, a consulting agreement instead of a purchase agreement\u2014and you may find out the hard way it doesn\u2019t hold up.\nAnd don\u2019t forget:\nGeographic scope needs to be defined (50 miles from where, exactly?)\n\nTime frame needs to make sense (hint: 5 years might not cover a 10-year SBA loan)\n\nActual clarity matters (your lawyer should be able to look at it and say, \u201cYes, you can do this\u201d or \u201cNo, you absolutely cannot\u201d)\n\nBut Wait, There\u2019s More (Nuance)\nLet\u2019s say your seller still wants to do their grandkid\u2019s taxes. Or help their favorite client until one of them dies (yes, that\u2019s a real quote I\u2019ve heard). That\u2019s fine. Just write it down. Include exceptions. Carve it out. Make it clear.\nBecause a good non-compete shouldn\u2019t feel like a straitjacket. It should feel like a well-fitting suit. Fits like a glove.\nWant to stop treating your non-compete like fine print and start using it like a power move?\nClick here to learn exactly how to draft one that holds up and keeps your deal clean.\nTo smarter deals (and fewer legal regrets),\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nFounder, Deal Academy\nP.S. If you\u2019ve got an upcoming transaction and you\u2019re not sure if your non-compete is worth the paper it\u2019s printed on, let\u2019s fix that before someone starts poaching your clients.\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2026\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
